      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-18_WidnesExaminer_art0015" n="art0015">
        <head>USEFrL AND BECOMING HAT.</head>
        <p>A USEFrL AND BECOMING HAT.</p>
        <p>/hry smart and weful, as well as most be- coming, is the modish little hat which forms the subject of our sketch. Though dressy enough for regular afternoon wear, this pretty chapeau is quite plain enough for every day morning use, and is most practical in both shape and trim- ming. The straw is of a coarse, strong, and yet</p>
        <p>r</p>
        <p>fairly supple weave, and is dyed a particularly good shade of Saxe-blue. The shape is somewhat suggestive of a sailor a round crown, and slightly upturned brim also of round shape. A wide velvet ribbon, sui,de-brown in colour, is folded round the crown and tied in a loose bow in front. From this bow spring beautiful "made" wings of ntingled shades of blue, brown, and ivory.</p>
