      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-18_WidnesExaminer_art0152" n="art0152">
        <head>KILLED BY A FURNITURE VAN.</head>
        <p>KILLED BY A FURNITURE VAN.</p>
        <p>A man named R. Humphreys, a native of Wigan, met with a fatal accident at Connah's Quay on Tuesday night. Humphreys, who WAS about 23 years of age, and belonged to the Royal Welsh Fusiliers, was tramping from Wigan into Wales. When nearing the Quay he was given a lift on a furniture van, and it is surmised that while asleep he fell off the van and was run over, as his body was found on the road near the Quay Church, with one side of his face crushed in.</p>
