        <p>I really hardly know what I am, after looking An Actual Excess of 13xIPurts• through them all. I hope to receive a few So that we arrive at an excess not of imports, but more during the present week. I shall then of exports. The, balance £57,000,000 is a rough award the prize. answers The a estimate of the sums left abroad in 1907 as an addi- Ithe i ilaluestaionds tor Eafszteerneaxtre ( ion to our oversee investments. That is to say, cweek.otng linwanwte some more award eoni). How to instead of the world being less indebted to us it is spend Easter Monday"; don't forget, and let becoming more indebted to us every year. - me have a lot of replies during the coming week. In another way the above tables will be found °' Further down these columns you will find a instructive. They help us to form an idea of the letter from a new member living in Gibraltar. true magnitude of our fiaancial, shipping, and com- I was most pleased to hear from Winnie Noll ; living t shows mercial relations with the world at larg Wes tall; Surely no long tdwte narees.nolt etriir vietteni b . one can contemplate the magnificent totals which come those more vin ore leg a wts tters from distances. °member, and I represent our transactions with people outside these hope she will try and send me a picture post- islands without reflecting thht a fiscal system which teard. J had quite a pkleaslanft eutrpirise a shotrt has led to such results cannot be the olish and ntitene isoirnce n-t-ya Ipaorogre settienldfureno cl hla c I thagnkammeoso fu t ruinous thing which Protectionists represent it to be heartily any members for their kindness. I If Free Trade meant ruin,—if it were an anti•national. can assure them that many little children will policy, its results could not be what they are after ,b. most pleased to receive these garments. . The following members' names were pinned to two generations of practice. the contents of the sack :—Annie York, Ruby Hart, Katie Doubleday, Maggie Faulkner