        <p>Jear U Ned,—Mrs. Wells said I was to write and/tell you that we have sent off a sack of clothes. All the children thank you very much for their boxes of chocolate. Mrs. Wells has been too busy to write before to you. We are sending you some drawings of yourself. I am afraid some of them will make you smile. The toys will follow in a few days. r 4 MARY RIISHBY. [My most grateful thanks to' Mrs. Wells for her kindness in arranging for the above-men- tioned gifts for the poor children.—UNCLE NED.]</p>
