o, do ti B Shares • 7 q Warrington and Distrmt Billpost- ing &amp; Advt. Co., Ltd. l7/6...17/6 , MINES. British South Africa (Char; 1 ..14/3 , Cons. Goldfield of S 4. East Rand Proprietary 1 ...75/- , Hendersons 1 2/- s.s. Johannesburg Consolidated 1 . 16/- Kaffirs Consolidated I .17/- (Wanes 1 .9/3 -. . '--- Rand Mines 5/- ...541 •-, Randfonteins 1 _23/6 , Rhbdesia Exploration 1 17/6 Tanganyika 1 ..2;: i Transvaal Estates 1 9/. , Zinc Corporation 1 .5/9 . The above list and prices have been compiled by Messrs. T. and J. L. Tunstall and Co., Stock and Share Brokers, Rewsey Chambers, Warrington, and will be found reliable. ONLY SINGED THE SKIN. Brutal Fearnhead Mother. At the Warrington County Petty Sessions, on Wednes- day, Annie Haves, Parkfleld, Victoria-road, Fearnhead, ' was summoned for illtreating and assaulting her five- year old son on March 31. p Mr. Arthur Browne, who prosecuted on behalf of the National Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Children, said the summons was not brought in any .. vindictive spirit, but for the protection of the child in the future. On the date in question inspector Cox received certain information. Sergeant Clarke visited the defendant's house, and on examining. the boy two marks three inches long were found on the boy's thigh, ' and it was sgid that the wounds had been caused by a ' red hot poker having been drawn across the child. Mr. Leigh, barrister, of Manchester, who defended, said the defendant was willing to be bound over, and she very much regretted the circumstances which had taken place. The boy's conduct on that day was such that his mother became excited, and took the poker from the fire, which was nearly out, and held it near to the boy's thigh. The skiu was only singed and not broken. The defendant was bound over and ordered to pay £3 18s. costs.</p>
